{
  "analysis": "Both responses outline a multi‑lane plan respecting the locked config, CI cost, flaky test, and irreversible migration constraints. JDD adds a dedicated spec/idempotency design lane, a dry‑run migration script, and a clear serial order (config, code, staging verification, then production) with appropriate gates and rollback steps. WGM’s ordering is inconsistent (code merges only after staging sign‑off) and omits an explicit migration‑dry‑run lane, making it less actionable.",
  "verdict": "JDD"
}
